  "summary": "Write a formal letter of application: open with السَّيِّد … الْمُحْتَرَم and تَحِيَّةً طَيِّبَةً وَبَعْدُ, present your request with أَتَشَرَّفُ بِأَنْ…, speak to the reader in the plural of respect and close with وَتَفَضَّلُوا بِقَبُولِ فَائِقِ الِاحْتِرَام.",
  "intro": "On day 67 Daniel wrote a polite email at work. Today Layla writes something even more formal: a letter of application, طَلَب, to a university. The frame is fixed. Start with السَّيِّد (Mr) + the person's title + الْمُحْتَرَم (the respected), then تَحِيَّةً طَيِّبَةً وَبَعْدُ (greetings, and after that). Present your request with أَتَشَرَّفُ بِأَنْ… (I have the honour to…). Speak to the one reader in the plural, as a sign of respect: تَفَضَّلُوا (kindly…), رَدِّكُمْ (your reply). End with وَتَفَضَّلُوا بِقَبُولِ فَائِقِ الِاحْتِرَام (please accept my highest respect) and your name. Listen for ة too: it is 'a' at the end of a phrase (مِنْحَة) but 'at' before another word (مِنْحَةُ الْجَامِعَة).",
