    "culture": "In the Arab world official letters still follow an old, fixed frame, and readers notice when it is missing. Writing to one official in the plural (تَفَضَّلُوا, رَدِّكُمْ, بِجَامِعَتِكُمْ) is normal and polite, not a mistake. Many letters put the subject on its own line, like الْمَوْضُوع: طَلَبُ مِنْحَة, and end with وَتَفَضَّلُوا بِقَبُولِ فَائِقِ الِاحْتِرَام, the Arabic 'Yours faithfully', before the name and the signature.",
